pageType: final
background:
  type: image
  src: media/template-blue-abstract.png
  fit: {mode: fill}
notes: |
  Timing: about 70 seconds.

  I ended with a four-second looping parallax study. The code assigns a simple vertical depth proxy, so lower and slightly more central regions move more strongly than distant regions. The virtual camera follows a smooth sine-and-cosine loop, and each frame remaps the image with reflected borders. This is a heuristic 2.5D effect, not CNN depth estimation. It feels like entering the picture because differential motion separates the image into depth layers: foreground figures drift, while the central doorway remains comparatively stable and acts like a visual anchor. I want to end with one sentence: every way of seeing has a bottleneck. The network preserves geometry; I preserve the history and meaning attached to the line.
